event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":89,"item_id":"rs_0f38df89155e76c2016acad0e939bc81949bd00d22c5eaebce","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering simple SSR forms**\n\nI’m thinking about implementing simple server-side rendered (SSR) forms that handle POST requests and redirect with any invalid inputs prompting a 400 HTML alert. The goal is to ensure accessibility without needing JavaScript, relying on just HTML and CSS for compatibility across browsers. Numeric IDs are part of the plan, and I’ll conduct tests using a temporary SQLite setup to help ease the process. Luckily, I have enough time to cover everything!"}

